        "question_type": "Objective",
        "exam_year": "2009",
        "question_text": "<p>For the reaction: $N_2(g) + 3H_2(g) \\rightleftharpoons 2NH_3(g)$, what is the effect of increasing the pressure on the equilibrium position?</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>According to Le Chatelier's Principle, increasing the pressure shifts the equilibrium position to the side with fewer moles of gas to reduce the pressure. In this reaction, the left side has 4 moles of gas ($1 N_2 + 3 H_2$), and the right side has 2 moles of gas ($2 NH_3$). Thus, the equilibrium shifts to the right, favoring the formation of $NH_3$.</p>",
        "reference_passage": null,
        "novel": null,
        "comments_count": 0,
        "options": [
